// OPTIONAL MODULE (disabled) — "decline smoothing" via WorldDefinition floors.
//
// This is the native-script equivalent of the ORIGINAL AUTHOR'S OWN disabled
// balance module (balance_patch.lua in BalancedTraders UE4SS, which shipped
// with BalanceEnabled = false): raising the lower bounds of the dynamic
// price multipliers from -1.0 to -0.25 so the saturation/liquidity drop can
// never fully zero out a price.
//
// In AngelScript this needs no runtime hook — a compile-time
// ReplaceParentClass override of the script-defined UDefaultWorldDefinition
// is enough, which also makes it multi-mod-safe on the current build.
//
// WHY IT IS DISABLED BY DEFAULT (matching the original author's choice):
// unlike the trophy curve, these floors apply to EVERY item category and to
// buy prices too — food, potions, weapons included. Enable only if you want
// the whole economy flattened above a -25% dynamic discount.
//
// To enable: rename this file to WorldDefinitionFloors.as
// (this file is not compiled in its .disabled state).

UCLASS(meta = (ReplaceParentClass))
class UDefaultWorldDefinition_BalancedTradersFloors : UDefaultWorldDefinition
{
	default m_RegionalMultiplierMin = -0.25f;
	default m_LiquidityMultiplierMin = -0.25f;
}
